   ideas into a more beautiful and useful place. Also, thank you to Suhee
   and Henri for their suggestions, to David Maddox at The Nature of Cities
   for his constant support and guidance, and to all of the individuals
   involved in the projects themselves. The examples explored in this
   article could not have been accomplished without collaboration and
   support from the communities in which they took place. We would like to
   make known our deep gratitude for those communities and individuals. The
   film, Final Straw: Food, Earth, Happiness was produced on a shoestring
   budget, with support of hundreds of individuals and dozens of
   institutions and community organizations. We would like to recognize the
   extraordinary support of Yoshikazu Kawaguchi and Larry Korn, two of our
